file construction/REDS.md %501, booked at 497 after a fetch and moved three times as peers published 497 through 500 against earlier stamps
obs THE NUMBER MOVED AGAIN, AND THE STAMP DID NOT. I read --next at 14:28 and it answered 497; by the time the second rebase ran, a peer had published their own %497 stamped 20260906.131501 against my 20260906.142051, and two more rows besides. The earlier stamp keeps the number, mine was unshared, so mine moved to %500 -- and on the very next pull a THIRD peer's %500, stamped 20260906.133957, took that too, so mine is %501. Four numbers in one round. I renumbered by targeted replacement over five named sites each time and checked the peer's four %497 and %498 mentions were untouched before writing -- %484's erratum is that a renumber is a rename and a rename sweeps only what it owns. The fourteenth firing of the card's open question, and the second time in two laps my own number moved twice in one round.
file construction/ITINERARY.md the DIFFUSER block folded and rewritten; %492's recital to its shelf
recommend keep-going -- the next lap in this lane is the one number this finding names and cannot supply: how much of the 3.50x gap any real degree-6 construction on 720 points actually recovers. The floor bounds the room from above; the degree-diameter problem is open, and the honest next move is to build a search that exhibits the best degree-6 graph it can find at that size and reports its diameter, so the gap stops being an upper bound and starts being a measured distance.
